// generated by plugin/scripts/build.mjs from cli/src (piezas 0.7.4); do not edit by hand
// Part of the piezas CLI (see index.js): the testing gate.
//
// Every approved scenario in SPEC.md becomes a check the app must pass before
// it is shared. This module owns that loop end to end:
//
//   scenarios -> a failing placeholder test per scenario (never overwritten)
//   -> a static "is this a real test?" check -> the run (one automatic retry)
//   -> per-scenario results with one plain sentence per failure
//   -> a record bound to the code (.piezas/test-attestation.json, 24h)
//   -> the deploy stop with the owner's three choices.
//
// Two audiences, kept apart on purpose. Everything in OWNER_TEXT is read by a
// non-technical business owner (directly, or relayed by their AI tool) and is
// scanned for jargon by a unit test. Reasons, file names and repair hints for
// the AI live in the JSON result and in files under .piezas/.
